From: MeizIshanDev <mezan@meshan.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] fog-0960: touch: Novatek IC on GPIO SPI, firmware and touch events

Measured on the phone: QUP0 SE0 has its FIFO interface disabled, and the IC
answers on GPIO SPI with MISO/MOSI/CLK/CS on GPIO 0-3, ID 0b xx xx 25 65 03.
Load the firmware the way nt36525b_spi does (hardware CRC, NT36672A register
map), from /sweet-touch in the ADT (mkpayload.py --touch-fw). Read touch frames
as nvt_ts_work_func does and report them through sweet_hid_touch. The rising-edge
IRQ is polled from the TLMM's latch, with a slow timed read as a fallback.
GPIO 36 (vibrator) is not touched.

---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
index 370d18b..11a7608 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -1,11 +1,21 @@
 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * topaz (SM6225): FocalTech FT5452 at 0x38 on QUP0 SE2, IRQ GPIO80, reset
- * GPIO86, AVDD enable GPIO36 (no regulator), values from topaz-woa
- * TopazTouch. Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one
- * thread. Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * fog (Redmi 10C, SM6225) touch: Novatek IC on bit-banged SPI, firmware, touch events.
+ *
+ * Measured on the phone: QUP0 SE0 has its FIFO interface disabled (GSI DMA only,
+ * behind the SMMU), so SPI mode 0 is driven by hand on GPIO 0-3. Chip ID
+ * 0b xx xx 25 65 03: Android's trim table gives the NT36672A register map and
+ * hardware CRC. The flow follows nt36525b_spi (nvt_download_firmware_hw_crc):
+ * the firmware goes to the IC's SRAM and is lost at power off.
+ *
+ * mkpayload.py --touch-fw puts the firmware in the ADT (/sweet-touch "firmware"),
+ * so that it stays out of this repository. Touch frames follow nvt_ts_work_func.
+ * The IRQ is a rising edge: the TLMM latches it in the pin's status register with
+ * no GIC interrupt, and a slow timed read covers an IRQ that never comes.
+ * Lines contain "TOUCH": read them with the shim's log viewer.
+ *
+ * GPIO 36 is the vibrator on fog: never touch it. GPIO 80 is only read.
+ * GPIO 86 (reset) is left alone, as Android does (NVT_TOUCH_SUPPORT_HW_RST 0),
+ * unless boot-arg sweettouchrst=1. Boot-arg sweetspidelay=N: N us per half clock.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
@@ -16,85 +26,107 @@
 #include <kern/sched_prim.h>
 #include <machine/machine_routines.h>
 #include <pexpert/pexpert.h>
